  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Guduru Dhanujaya vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 21 August, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4871 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "1. The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.165 of 2019 of Chapadu Police Station, YSR Kadapa District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 328 of IPC and Sections 57, 58 R/w. Sections 26 and 30 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short, 'the FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 25.07.2019 at 06.30 p.m., when the complainant along with his staff including the panchayatdars was proceeding towards Peerlachavidi of Chapadu village, found the petitioner carrying business in the kirana shop in front of Peerlachavidi and on interrogation the petitioner confessed to have possessing the banned tobacco products for sale in his kirana shop and as the accused voluntarily confessed to have been engaged in the business of prohibited tobacco products, seized the same, registered F.I.R., remanded him to judicial custody for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
